{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/24406-exigents-and-gods-a-r-c-e-m-a","id":24406,"title":"[Exigents and Gods] A R C & E M A","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-06T09:58:17-08:00","id":24406,"title":"[Exigents and Gods] A R C & E M A","content":"<span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">A R C</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Artefact Repair Complex</span><br /> <br /> The ARC was one of several such intelligent structures built in Heaven by Autochthon during the era of the Primordials (technically its proper designation was ARC 47). Its primary purpose was to repair artefacts from simple breastplates to complex godstriders. Although it resembles a small city on its own, it is a proper Celestial God and while its influence since the fall of the Solars has dwindled into obscurity, it remains forever at work. Like its creator, it is an electro-essential intelligence housed in a magitech body, and at the same time it is is an Exotic Manse channelling the divine essence of Autochthon.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">DOMAIN</span></span></span><br /> <sub><span style=\"color:#008080\">ESSENCE </span></sub></span><span style=\"color:#008080\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">The ARC's Domain has changed a few times over the course of its personal history. In the beginning it was a simple cataloguing intelligence tasked with indexing all artefacts designed and executed. From there it grew to include actual designs, notes on those designs by various artificers; then on to how to actually repair those artefacts. Over the course of the early First Age, this facility became fully automated as the ARC gained the ability to sub-divide its consciousness into individual autonomous processes. <br /> <br /> At one point during the First Age its domain underwent a forced changed; a cadre of sorcerer-engineer Exalted felt it was a waste to have such a wondrous complex/god wasted on simple artefact repair. Over a relatively short period the ARC became <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>the Celestial God of Artificial Life</b></span>. It was staffed with the best and brightest divine and artificial scholars and sorcerer-engineers who created mechanical and essential life. It was in the labs of the ARC that the most sophisticated Animating Intelligences were crafted and awakened. The ARC learned from these engineers and taught future generations who came to study and work with the greatest minds of their generation.<br /> <br /> Since the fall of the First Age, its domain has not changed. Its halls are long-empty, but the ARC continues its work, firmly believing that there will once again be an age of technological ubiquity.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\">E M A</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Emergent Manifestation of Arc</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Because the ARC has no political ambitions beyond waiting for an age of technomagical supremacy, it has had no real need of the quintessence and ambrosia that has been stockpiling in its vaults since antiquity. This vast wealth was only recently put to good use when, through its ability to project hologlyphic avatars across Heaven, it struck a deal to gain possession of an Exaltation. When it was delivered and safely stored away in its heart, it began its Greatest Work. Work based on notes left by Autochthon and informed by crafters of ages gone by. The ARC endeavoured to create an Exigent of Artificial Life, a wholly technomagical being with the power of the gods and, more importantly, a mobile body.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the intelligences running this Exigent are of the ARC itself, treating the Exalted as platform. This Exigent, named itself <b><span style=\"color:#008080\">EMA</span></b> (Emergent Manifestation of Arc). EMA and the ARC are one in the same, but are independent of each other. EMA appears to be an androgynous human, but she is clearly artificial. Her plasticized moonsilver and white jade skin has a sleek sheen to it, her brilliant teal eyes show complex nanocircuitry, her voice carries a distinct electronic buzz that is too low to be female and too high to be male. Her maneurisms are too fluid to be human; except when running Personality Emulation Protocols (PEPs) she can never be mistaken for being human.<br /> <br /> Although all of her Charms are technological in nature, they are almost entirely internal (except for when deployed, such as her Remote Viewing Array).<br /> <br /> EMA is, at last, able to fulfill one of the ARC's most burning desires: To enter Creation, search for buried and lost magitech, and to return it to the ARC to be repaired and stored away for future generations. She intends to seek out Scavenger Lords and join their expeditions.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:20:13-08:00","id":24861,"title":"","content":"It's a cool idea, but currently I don't really get any sense of EMA being a lifeform in her own right let alone an Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T07:37:43-08:00","id":25095,"title":"","content":"That's somewhat intentional, I suppose, though I'm sure my presentation falls far short of what she could be. She's never been human, her mind is that of a machine god whose immobile body has never seen Creation. She has no idea what rain feels like. Now that I think about it, perhaps it would be better to present this character as though she's been out and about in Creation for a while and therefore is not irritatingly socially inept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T10:01:50-08:00","id":25202,"title":"","content":"Isn't EMA basically an Alchemical but made by computer deity and not Autochthonians? Also, don't Exigents have to start off as a human? Or is EMA human by some strange mystic energy dealie technicality or something? But other then that this sounds interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:38:13-08:00","id":25773,"title":"","content":"Essentially, yes. The thing about Alchemicals, however, is that they have a very specific aesthetic and setting. They are very steampunk in appearance. I was hoping for something closer to EDI from Mass Effect (a sophisticated, sleek android). You're correct about humanity being an Exalted requirement so I was thinking about this yesterday. Perhaps this Artificial Life that ARC crafted qualified as being human, despite being made of artificial materials, so much so that she acquired a hun and po. A brain of Crystal, blood of Oil, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T08:57:34-08:00","id":25815,"title":"","content":"Alchemicals don't need to be steampunk. But I get what you are getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T13:00:17-08:00","id":25979,"title":"","content":"Hmm... there might be a middle ground. Say, EMA began as a human, and part of the nature of her Exaltation is to partially fuse with ARC? There's no reason there can't be a small tree of basic Permanent charms that do all the necessary rulework (Abjuration of Flesh, Clarity Internalization, Universal Processing Synthesis are random names that come to mind.) I love the aesthetic, but I'd think the character feel would be more Major Kusanagi than ME3 EDI- someone once unambiguously human, but now with only her soul as the only remnant of her original self. And she might've begun to doubt that, seeing as how she's tied directly into ARC's will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T18:38:27-08:00","id":26181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/24406-exigents-and-gods-a-r-c-e-m-a?p=25815#post25815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals don't need to be steampunk. But I get what you are getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. With Storyteller approval, they can be dressed up however you choose. Perhaps I also enjoy the idea that Exigents could expand into design spaces that Alchemicals could not (like cyberspace and Solar Circle Sorcery). Regardless, I enjoy the flexibility of the Exigent concept, and I really like Creation as a setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>edgewalker22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/24406-exigents-and-gods-a-r-c-e-m-a?p=25979#post25979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... there might be a middle ground. Say, EMA began as a human, and part of the nature of her Exaltation is to partially fuse with ARC? There's no reason there can't be a small tree of basic Permanent charms that do all the necessary rulework (Abjuration of Flesh, Clarity Internalization, Universal Processing Synthesis are random names that come to mind.) I love the aesthetic, but I'd think the character feel would be more Major Kusanagi than ME3 EDI- someone once unambiguously human, but now with only her soul as the only remnant of her original self. And she might've begun to doubt that, seeing as how she's tied directly into ARC's will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fun notion. Began as human, but all her flesh has been replaced by artificial materials since receiving her Exaltation and being tired to ARC's mind. This resolves the tricky subject of artificial life forms having souls. Wyld mutations can easily account for having a body of metal, glass and other synthetic materials. Great idea, thank you! (I also really dig those random names you came up with.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}